{
  "name": "What to Do When You Notice a Persistent Leak",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "Finding a persistent leak can be super frustrating, but acting fast can prevent a small issue from becoming a huge headache. First off, try to find the source of the leak and if it's from a pipe, shut off the water supply to that area or even your whole house if you can't isolate it. That's step one in preventing more damage! Next, try to catch the water with buckets or towels to minimize any mess. Once you've got the immediate situation under control, assess how serious it seems. Is it a slow drip or a steady stream? Is it near electrical outlets? If it's a minor drip and you're comfortable, you might try a temporary fix, but honestly, for anything more serious, or if you're not sure, it's really best to call in a professional. They can properly diagnose the root cause and make sure the repair is done right, preventing future problems and potential water damage down the line. Don't let a small leak turn into a costly mold or structural issue. When in doubt, a quick call to HH Remodeling LLC can give you peace of mind and get things fixed properly. We're here to help folks in Denver, Centennial, and all the surrounding areas, so don't hesitate to reach out.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    }
  ],
